Thanks all. Writing down what we know so far, proper RCA to follow.

What happened: The month-end report batch ran inside orders-worker and loaded=
 every order of the month into memory. Workers hit their 512Mi limit and were=
 killed again and again for just over an hour.
Impact: Confirmations up to 40 minutes late for about 5,200 orders. No orders=
 lost.

Timeline (UTC):
2026-06-30 23:15 Month-end batch started inside orders-worker. None.
2026-06-30 23:20 Alert OrdersWorkerOOMKilled fired. On-call restarted the wor=
kers.
2026-06-30 23:48 Workers killed again within minutes of each restart. Paged t=
he orders team.
2026-07-01 00:12 Orders team found the batch loading the whole month into mem=
ory. Disabled the batch flag and restarted the workers.
2026-07-01 00:25 Workers stable and the backlog cleared. Closed the incident.

Root cause: The month-end batch loaded all orders of the month into worker me=
mory at once. The batch ran inside orders-worker, so its memory use killed th=
e order consumer too.
Fix: Restarted the workers with the month-end batch disabled, then ran the ba=
tch on a separate job.

Follow ups:
- Move the month-end batch to its own scheduled job. (Orders team)
- Read orders in pages of 1,000 in the batch. (Orders team)

